; 54-indent.kurt

; `indent` is a toggle (`indent on` / `indent off`) that switches on
; indentation-based block structure in the *interactive shell* -- letting
; you paste multi-line, indented file content straight into the prompt, and
; enabling `done`/`break` (lessons 24-25) to close blocks explicitly.  A
; `.kurt` *file* always uses real indentation regardless of this setting, so
; toggling it here has no visible effect -- this lesson exists mainly so the
; keyword isn't a mystery when you meet it in the shell.

indent               ; reports the current setting
indent on
indent
indent off
